kernelbase: OutputDebugString without a listener; ntdll: NtFlushBuffersFile notes for FEX.

In b162 (Proton d2r11) D2R's character select screen had a 70-115 ms frame every 10 s
(t=651, 660, 670, 680, 690). In each of those seconds the Battle.net SDK thread (BGS_Thread)
wrote ~600 log lines with OutputDebugStringW, the wineserver got 590-672 open_mapping requests,
and the main thread waited 50-90 ms in RtlAcquireSRWLockExclusive.

Wine's OutputDebugStringW raises DBG_PRINTEXCEPTION_WIDE_C, calls OutputDebugStringA, which
raises DBG_PRINTEXCEPTION_C, and then calls OpenFileMappingW("DBWIN_BUFFER"): one wineserver
request that fails when no debug monitor (DebugView) runs. Without a debugger both exceptions
are caught again by their own __EXCEPT. On ARM64EC each one also converts the context to x64
and goes through the emulator's ResetToConsistentState.

- The two exceptions are raised only when something but that __EXCEPT could see them: a
  debugger (PEB BeingDebugged; Wine's NtRaiseException sends a debug event only then), a
  vectored exception handler (they run before the frame handlers, so a protection's VEH still
  sees every message), or, on ARM64EC, a patched x64 KiUserExceptionDispatcher or a wow64 hook.
  ntdll's new __wine_d2r_exception_watchers() answers that (1 debugger, 2 VEH, 4 x64 hook,
  0 nobody). When it says 0, the __EXCEPT would have run and nothing else, so leaving the
  raise out changes nothing anyone can see. OutputDebugStringW still calls the exported
  OutputDebugStringA, as in stock, for hooks on it.
- After a look for DBWIN_BUFFER found none, the next look is 1 s later instead of on the next
  call (a monitor started in between misses up to 1 s of messages). While a monitor runs,
  every call looks, as in stock.
WINE_D2R_ODS_FAST=0 turns both off. The switch and ntdll's exports are looked up once in
kernelbase's DllMain, since GetProcAddress takes the loader lock and OutputDebugString never did.

Counters for FEX in __wine_d2r_server_calls_ext (now 4360 bytes, 545 ULONG64), on with the
request counts (WINE_D2R_CALL_COUNTS):
- at byte 3728, written by kernelbase (found with GetProcAddress, so the same copy as the unix
  side and FEX use): ods_w_calls, ods_w_ns, ods_a_calls, ods_a_ns, ods_max_ns, ods_raised,
  ods_dbwin_opens, ods_dbwin_skipped (ULONG64), ods_last_tid, ods_watchers (ULONG).
  A calls made by W count as A calls too, and W time includes them.
- at byte 3800, NtFlushBuffersFile(Ex) (BGS_Thread also flushes its log file; FEX can now see
  whether main waits behind those fsyncs): flush_calls, flush_ns, flush_max_ns,
  flush_other_calls, flush_other_ns, flush_next; flush_tid[8] at 3848 (tid, count, ns, max_ns,
  last_end_ns, 32 bytes, first 8 threads that flush); flush[8] at 4104 (seq, tid, status,
  kind, start_ns, ns, 32 bytes, the latest 8 calls, same seq rule as the registry notes).
  Times are CLOCK_MONOTONIC ns, like FEX's own clock.

Tests: model test of OutputDebugStringA/W (/home/claude/pw/odstest, the patch's own function
text with mocked calls): 20000 random A/W calls with a monitor coming and going, per mode: no
watchers (0 raises, 5973 looks instead of 20000), VEH (every raise seen, 29943 as stock),
switch off (stock counts), debugger (as stock), counters off, not set up (as stock); 0
differences in what a VEH, debugger or monitor gets except the documented 1 s; last error kept;
no GetProcAddress after set-up. Negative controls (always skip, never look again, 10 ms window,
A or W raising without watchers) caught. Flush notes
(/home/claude/pw/flushtest, the patch's own functions): 12 threads x 20000 calls x 40 rounds
with a reader thread checking the notes: 0 wrong counts or slots, 0 torn reads in 168 million;
negative controls (slot taken without compare-exchange, note written without the seq claim)
caught. PE side compiles for x86_64, i686, aarch64 and arm64ec with no new warnings.
---
diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
index e1784fc..c6dd8d4 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
@@ -176,6 +176,101 @@ static LONG WINAPI debug_exception_handler( EXCEPTION_POINTERS *eptr )
     return (rec->ExceptionCode == DBG_PRINTEXCEPTION_C) ? EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER : EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH;
 }
 
+/* d2r (fex-d2-reforged, patch 0015): OutputDebugString without a debugger or a debug monitor.
+ *
+ * Every OutputDebugStringW call raises DBG_PRINTEXCEPTION_WIDE_C and then, in
+ * OutputDebugStringA, DBG_PRINTEXCEPTION_C, each caught again by its own __EXCEPT when no
+ * debugger is attached, and then tries OpenFileMappingW("DBWIN_BUFFER"), a wineserver round
+ * trip that fails when no monitor (DebugView) runs. In b162 D2R's Battle.net SDK thread
+ * (BGS_Thread) made 590-838 such calls in one second every 10 s in the character screen, and
+ * the main thread had a 70-115 ms frame in each of those seconds. On ARM64EC every exception
+ * also converts the context to x64 and goes through the emulator's ResetToConsistentState.
+ * - The exceptions are raised only when something could see them: a debugger, a vectored
+ *   exception handler, or a hooked x64 KiUserExceptionDispatcher (ntdll's
+ *   __wine_d2r_exception_watchers). Otherwise only the __EXCEPT here would catch them, so
+ *   leaving them out changes nothing anyone can see.
+ * - After DBWIN_BUFFER was not found, it is looked for again after 1 s instead of on every
+ *   call (a monitor started meanwhile misses up to 1 s of messages).
+ * WINE_D2R_ODS_FAST=0 turns both off. Calls, time, raises and DBWIN lookups are counted in
+ * ntdll's __wine_d2r_server_calls_ext (at byte 3728) when the request counts are on. */
+#define D2R_EXT_SIZE     12          /* ULONG index of the export's size word (byte 48) */
+#define D2R_EXT_ODS      (3728 / 8)  /* ULONG64 index of ods_w_calls */
+#define D2R_EXT_ODS_END  3800        /* the build writes at least this much when the counters are on */
+
+enum { D2R_ODS_W_CALLS, D2R_ODS_W_NS, D2R_ODS_A_CALLS, D2R_ODS_A_NS, D2R_ODS_MAX_NS, D2R_ODS_RAISED,
+       D2R_ODS_DBWIN_OPENS, D2R_ODS_DBWIN_SKIPPED, D2R_ODS_LAST };
+
+struct d2r_ods
+{
+    ULONG64      *counts;   /* the ODS counters, NULL when off */
+    LARGE_INTEGER start;
+    ULONG         watchers; /* see __wine_d2r_exception_watchers; ~0 when unknown or switched off */
+    BOOL          fast;     /* WINE_D2R_ODS_FAST isn't 0 */
+};
+
+static LONG d2r_ods_state;                 /* 0 not set up, 1 on, 2 switched off */
+static ULONG (CDECL *d2r_ods_watchers)(void);
+static ULONG64 *d2r_ods_ext;               /* ntdll's __wine_d2r_server_calls_ext */
+static LONG d2r_dbwin_next;                /* GetTickCount() for the next DBWIN_BUFFER look, 0 = every call */
+
+/* from DllMain: GetProcAddress takes the loader lock, which OutputDebugString never does */
+void d2r_ods_init(void)
+{
+    HMODULE ntdll = GetModuleHandleW( L"ntdll.dll" );
+    char value[16];
+    DWORD len = GetEnvironmentVariableA( "WINE_D2R_ODS_FAST", value, sizeof(value) );
+
+    if (ntdll)
+    {
+        d2r_ods_watchers = (void *)GetProcAddress( ntdll, "__wine_d2r_exception_watchers" );
+        d2r_ods_ext = (ULONG64 *)GetProcAddress( ntdll, "__wine_d2r_server_calls_ext" );
+    }
+    WriteRelease( &d2r_ods_state, (len && len < sizeof(value) && value[0] == '0') ? 2 : 1 );
+}
+
+static void d2r_ods_begin( struct d2r_ods *ods )
+{
+    ULONG64 *ext;
+
+    /* not set up (no DllMain yet): as stock */
+    ods->fast = ReadAcquire( &d2r_ods_state ) == 1;
+    ods->watchers = (ods->fast && d2r_ods_watchers) ? d2r_ods_watchers() : ~0u;
+    ods->counts = NULL;
+    if ((ext = d2r_ods_ext) && ReadAcquire( (LONG *)ext ) == 1 &&
+        ((volatile ULONG *)ext)[D2R_EXT_SIZE] >= D2R_EXT_ODS_END)
+    {
+        ods->counts = ext + D2R_EXT_ODS;
+        NtQueryPerformanceCounter( &ods->start, NULL );
+    }
+}
+
+static void d2r_ods_count( struct d2r_ods *ods, unsigned int counter )
+{
+    if (ods->counts) InterlockedIncrement64( (LONG64 *)&ods->counts[counter] );
+}
+
+static void d2r_ods_end( struct d2r_ods *ods, BOOL wide )
+{
+    ULONG64 *c = ods->counts;
+    LARGE_INTEGER end;
+    LONG64 ns, max;
+
+    if (!c) return;
+    NtQueryPerformanceCounter( &end, NULL );
+    ns = (end.QuadPart - ods->start.QuadPart) * 100;  /* 100 ns ticks */
+    InterlockedIncrement64( (LONG64 *)&c[wide ? D2R_ODS_W_CALLS : D2R_ODS_A_CALLS] );
+    InterlockedExchangeAdd64( (LONG64 *)&c[wide ? D2R_ODS_W_NS : D2R_ODS_A_NS], ns );
+    max = ReadNoFence64( (LONG64 *)&c[D2R_ODS_MAX_NS] );
+    while (ns > max)
+    {
+        LONG64 prev = InterlockedCompareExchange64( (LONG64 *)&c[D2R_ODS_MAX_NS], ns, max );
+        if (prev == max) break;
+        max = prev;
+    }
+    WriteNoFence( (LONG *)&c[D2R_ODS_LAST], GetCurrentThreadId() );
+    WriteNoFence( (LONG *)&c[D2R_ODS_LAST] + 1, ods->watchers );
+}
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           OutputDebugStringA   (kernelbase.@)
  */
@@ -185,10 +280,17 @@ void WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH OutputDebugStringA( LPCSTR str )
     static HANDLE DBWinMutex = NULL;
     static BOOL mutex_inited = FALSE;
     BOOL caught_by_dbg = TRUE;
+    struct d2r_ods ods;
 
     if (!str) str = "";
     WARN( "%s\n", debugstr_a(str) );
 
+    d2r_ods_begin( &ods );
+    /* patch 0015: nobody but the __EXCEPT here could see it */
+    if (!ods.watchers) caught_by_dbg = FALSE;
+    else
+    {
+    d2r_ods_count( &ods, D2R_ODS_RAISED );
     /* raise exception, WaitForDebugEvent() will generate a corresponding debug event */
     __TRY
     {
@@ -202,7 +304,12 @@ void WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH OutputDebugStringA( LPCSTR str )
         caught_by_dbg = FALSE;
     }
     __ENDTRY
-    if (caught_by_dbg) return;
+    }
+    if (caught_by_dbg)
+    {
+        d2r_ods_end( &ods, FALSE );
+        return;
+    }
 
     /* send string to a system-wide monitor */
     if (!mutex_inited)
@@ -220,9 +327,18 @@ void WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH OutputDebugStringA( LPCSTR str )
 
     if (DBWinMutex)
     {
-        HANDLE mapping;
+        HANDLE mapping = NULL;
+        LONG next = ods.fast ? ReadNoFence( &d2r_dbwin_next ) : 0;
 
-        mapping = OpenFileMappingW( FILE_MAP_WRITE, FALSE, L"DBWIN_BUFFER" );
+        /* patch 0015: no monitor less than 1 s ago, don't look again yet */
+        if (next && (LONG)(GetTickCount() - next) < 0)
+            d2r_ods_count( &ods, D2R_ODS_DBWIN_SKIPPED );
+        else
+        {
+            d2r_ods_count( &ods, D2R_ODS_DBWIN_OPENS );
+            mapping = OpenFileMappingW( FILE_MAP_WRITE, FALSE, L"DBWIN_BUFFER" );
+            if (ods.fast) WriteNoFence( &d2r_dbwin_next, mapping ? 0 : (LONG)((GetTickCount() + 1000) | 1) );
+        }
         if (mapping)
         {
             LPVOID buffer;
@@ -264,6 +380,7 @@ void WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH OutputDebugStringA( LPCSTR str )
             CloseHandle( mapping );
         }
     }
+    d2r_ods_end( &ods, FALSE );
     SetLastError( last_error );
 }
 
@@ -280,14 +397,20 @@ void WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH OutputDebugStringW( LPCWSTR str )
 {
     UNICODE_STRING strW;
     STRING strA;
+    struct d2r_ods ods;
 
     WARN( "%s\n", debugstr_w(str) );
 
+    d2r_ods_begin( &ods );
     RtlInitUnicodeString( &strW, str );
     if (!RtlUnicodeStringToAnsiString( &strA, &strW, TRUE ))
     {
-        BOOL exc_handled;
+        BOOL exc_handled = FALSE;
 
+        /* patch 0015: raised only when something but the __EXCEPT here could see it */
+        if (ods.watchers)
+        {
+        d2r_ods_count( &ods, D2R_ODS_RAISED );
         __TRY
         {
             ULONG_PTR args[4];
@@ -303,12 +426,14 @@ void WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH OutputDebugStringW( LPCWSTR str )
             exc_handled = FALSE;
         }
         __ENDTRY
+        }
 
         if (!exc_handled)
             OutputDebugStringA( strA.Buffer );
 
         RtlFreeAnsiString( &strA );
     }
+    d2r_ods_end( &ods, TRUE );
 }
 
 
